Below is a quick summary of what’s happening and how we’re fixing it:

1. Bug summary  
   • In Scratch 3.0, when you create a new slider‐watcher (right‐click → “slider”), it always uses the hard-coded 0–100 range (via defaultProps in the SliderMonitor component), even if the VM has saved a different `sliderMin`/`sliderMax` (for example, when you import an old 2.0 project).  
   • We need to hoist any VM-provided `sliderMin`/`sliderMax` out of the raw monitor props and feed them into the React monitor component in place of its 0–100 defaults.

2. Root cause  
   • In `src/containers/monitor.jsx` we render `<MonitorComponent … min={this.props.min} max={this.props.max} …/>`, but never look for `this.props.sliderMin` or `sliderMax`.  
   • Because those never make it into the child component, `slider-monitor.jsx` simply falls back to its own defaultProps of 0 and 100.

3. Fix  
   • In the container, if the VM has provided `sliderMin`/`sliderMax` on the monitor object, use those; otherwise fall back to the existing `this.props.min`/`max`.  
   • Pass those computed `sliderMin`/`sliderMax` values into the child instead of the raw `this.props.min`/`max`.

